<template><main class="main-content"><div class="page-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">PROJECT NOTES</p><h1>About NetPulse</h1><p class="intro-copy">A focused workspace for understanding real protocol behavior.</p></div></div><section class="about-grid"><article class="about-card panel"><p class="eyebrow">THE PLATFORM</p><h2>Measure the difference, not the assumption.</h2><p>NetPulse is a PBL 2 Computer Networks application for comparing TCP and UDP performance through real local socket communication.</p></article><article class="about-card panel"><p class="eyebrow">HOW IT WORKS</p><h2>One workload, two transport models.</h2><p>The backend sends sequential JSON messages through a persistent TCP connection or UDP datagrams, measures client-side round-trip time, and reports delivery and throughput statistics.</p></article><article class="about-card panel"><p class="eyebrow">TECHNOLOGY</p><h2>Native where it matters.</h2><p>Vue 3 and Vite power the interface. Node.js and Express provide the API, with <code>node:net</code> for TCP and <code>node:dgram</code> for UDP.</p></article><article class="about-card panel"><p class="eyebrow">LIMITATIONS</p><h2>Interpret results in context.</h2><p>Measurements are application-level observations from the client. Throughput excludes protocol headers, and packet loss is not a direct physical-network loss measurement.</p></article></section></main></template>
